    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0943" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3459</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1929-06-25"
                            >June 25, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received July 9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 301</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of the treaty between Peru and Chile settling the Tacna-Arica
                        question.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d658-f1"/> It was handed to me by President
                    Leguia at Government Palace this morning, and it will be noted that there are
                    several changes from the text of the original agreement as proposed by President
                    Hoover.</p>
                <p>I am not sending an English translation because the Department has better
                    facilities therefor than the mission, and because the Spanish text of the
                    original agreement is already on file in Washington.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander P.
                    Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d658-f1" n="46" xml:id="d658-f1-content">
                <p>Signed June 3, 1929. For text, see League of Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">xciv</hi>, p. 402.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
